#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Idea]
// #title[Title]

In univalent mathematics there is an interesting way to think about groups.
Every #local("00GY")[pointed connected 1-type] carries a group structure in
natural way: The composition of paths in the loop space is associative and
every path is reversible. In fact every group arises as the loop space of some
pointed connected 1-type. We will use results from the #local("00D6")[Symmetry
Book] that explores this idea in great detail.

We give all the definitions necessary to state the #local("00HG")[Orbit
Stabilizer Theorem], which will help us prove the #local("00FY")[Class
Formula], an important tool for computing the #local("00ER")[groupoid
cardinality] of 1-types, which is key for decategorifying a lot of our constructions.
